  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An object of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> is attached to a spring and is made to oscillate with simple harmonic motion (SHM). The distance between the two maximum displacement positions of the object is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span>. The total energy of the spring is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span>. What is the total energy of the spring when the mass of the object is changed to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M}{4}\"></span> and the distance between the two maximum displacement positions is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6d\"></span>? </p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{2}E\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{9}{4}E\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4E\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"9E\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
